# Deploy (Raspberry Pi kiosks)

**Never ask for, store, or use SSH passwords** (or sudo passwords). Do not put secrets, private keys, or `authorized_keys` in the repo.

`npm run deploy` (`scripts/deploy.sh`) builds on Stue, then reboots **Stue, Entre, and Andre**. Andre has no app server; the reboot reloads Chromium on `http://192.168.68.91/andre`.

| Pi | Address | Role |
| -- | ------- | ---- |
| Stue | `pi@192.168.68.91` | Express + kiosk `/`. App: `/home/pi/Projects/homey-dashboard`. systemd: `dashboard.service` |
| Entre | `rpi@192.168.68.99` | Kiosk `/entre` only (no app server) |
| Andre (gang 2. etg) | `rpi@192.168.68.82` | Chromium on `http://192.168.68.91/andre` only (no app server). Fullscreen Chromium via systemd `dashboard.service` (`--start-fullscreen`, no `--kiosk`). `npm run deploy` reboots it after Stue is back (`SKIP_ANDRE=1` to skip) |

- **User deploys** from the Mac. SSH keys only, `BatchMode`. Mac and the main Pi must be on `main`; the Pi pulls `origin/main`.
- **Agents** do not SSH to the Pis unless the user explicitly asks. If they do, use `ssh -o BatchMode=yes` only. Never request a password or GitHub key passphrase, never run `ssh-copy-id`, never disable host-key checking.
